This software contains code adapted from the Wisconsin Card Sorting Task (WCST) project.

Original Project: WCST (PsychoPy edition)
Source URL: https://github.com/OttoKuosmanen/WCST
Original Authors: Otto Kuosmanen (Keijumies) and contributors
Original License: MIT (see `tasks/WCST/LICENSE`)

Reference:
- Esta A. Berg (1948). A Simple Objective Technique for Measuring Flexibility in Thinking.
  The Journal of General Psychology, 39(1), 15-22.
  https://doi.org/10.1080/00221309.1948.9918159

Modifications made in this repository:

1. Integration into MeRID task framework
   - Integrated WCST into the local multi-task psychometric test suite.
   - Added standardized task launch and local participant output structure.

2. Configuration and runtime control
   - Added YAML-based configuration loading (`configs/config.yaml` and `configs/experiment.yaml`).
   - Added command-line argument support for participant folder/output routing.

3. Multilingual and text rendering adaptations
   - Added language-specific instruction loading from local `languages/` resources.
   - Added support for right-to-left scripts and font fallback handling.

4. Data and file handling updates
   - Adapted trial/instruction table loading to support local spreadsheet/CSV inputs.
   - Updated result and log export paths for local offline administration.

This NOTICE is provided to preserve attribution for the original WCST implementation
while documenting adaptations made for this repository.
